# chorus golden vector: session refused (a v1 peer), protocol v2 message type 0x23.
#
# Committed, and never written by a test. Any implementation of chorus protocol v2 must
# produce these exact bytes from the canonical input in session_refused_v1_peer.fields, and recover
# exactly those fields from them (docs/protocol.md, "Version 2").
#
# Format: whitespace separated hex bytes, '#' starts a comment.

# frame header: type 0x23, payload length 94 (0x005E), big-endian
23 00 5E

# reason = 1 (protocol_version)
01

# detail: length 91, then UTF-8, exactly what a v2 server sends a peer whose first frame is a v1 time_sync
00 5B 72 65 66 75 73 65 64 20 61 20 63 68 6F 72
75 73 20 70 72 6F 74 6F 63 6F 6C 20 76 31 20 70
65 65 72 20 28 69 74 73 20 66 69 72 73 74 20 66
72 61 6D 65 20 77 61 73 20 74 69 6D 65 5F 73 79
6E 63 29 3B 20 74 68 69 73 20 73 69 64 65 20 73
70 65 61 6B 73 20 76 32 20 6F 6E 6C 79
